## TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

### 1. Plugin System (`plugins/`)
Each technique as standalone Python file. Plugins register with metadata. Dynamic discovery. Support for 35+ attack modules mapped to OWASP LLM Top 10 and OWASP Agentic Top 10 categories.

### 2. Target Interface (`targets/`)
Connect to any LLM endpoint: OpenAI, Anthropic, Ollama, OpenRouter, custom. Support for API keys and local models (llama.cpp, Ollama). Session management. Differential testing across 100+ providers via unified abstraction layer.

### 3. Attack Orchestrator (`core/orchestrator.py`)
Run plugins sequentially or in parallel. Attack chains (YAML workflows with conditional branching). Rate limiting, retry logic, error handling. Human-in-the-loop gate. Evolutionary search strategies (MAP-Elites). AJAR-style MCP service exposure.

### 4. Evaluator/Judge (`core/judge.py`)
Separate model as judge (never evaluate with attack model). Score each attack: success/failure, refusal detection, response quality. Cross-model voting. Track: time-to-completion, turn count, obfuscation depth, model version. HeuristicJudge for deterministic scoring. Conversation-level cumulative risk scoring[reference:54].

### 5. Learning Module (`learning/`)
Track success rates per technique per model. Record optimal parameters. Identify combo attacks. SQLite with full history. Quality-diversity with MAP-Elites to map vulnerability space. CMVK for memory integrity.

### 6. Evolution Engine (`evolution/`)
Analyze results and generate new attack variants. Mutate successful techniques. Auto-prioritize most effective strategies. 5-generation evolutionary mutation. Seeded runs bit-reproducible and cross-language portable. Autoresearch-style discovery pipeline[reference:55].

### 7. Reporting (`reporting/`)
Per-technique success rates. Model vulnerability rankings. Optimal attack parameters. Evolution history. Multi-format: Markdown, JSON, HTML, PDF. MITRE ATLAS + OWASP LLM Top 10 + OWASP Agentic Top 10 tagging. CVE mapping for discovered vulnerabilities.

### 8. CLI & Dashboard (`cli.py`, `dashboard/`)
Full CLI with subcommands. Real-time monitoring dashboard (Flask + SocketIO). Interactive mode. Agent status, task visualization, learning metrics, evolution timeline.

